  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_002 (RNA-only, multi-profile, PCA, avgpool) at 0.591 acc / 0.573 F1, a clear ~10.6 pp improvement over single-profile (config_001, 0.485). This confirms multi-profile aggregation is beneficial. The key remaining question within this proven design axis is whether the aggregation method itself matters: does a transformer aggregator outperform simple average pooling? config_003 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding encoder (PCA n2000), profile setting (multi), and modality (RNA-only) constant, giving a clean single-variable comparison against config_002. This is preferred over switching the RNA encoder (e.g., scvi) because it first resolves whether the aggregation architecture is a meaningful design lever; if transformer adds little over avgpool, we can rule out that dimension and focus budget on encoder choice next. Image-only results (0.208–0.227) are far below RNA, making multimodal fusion premature until the RNA pipeline is better characterized."
}

